  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length set at The Vogue in Indianapolis, Indiana, on Saturday, October 16, 2021 [1]. This recording, captured and transferred by Liz Hamilton, documents 24 songs over 107 minutes, representing show 327 of 467 in the archive’s collection for the band [1][2]. The setlist features a mix of tracks from various albums, including “Parisian Enclave” from *Dark in Here* and “Letter from Belgium” from *We Shall All Be Healed* [1]. Notably, “Parisian Enclave” and “When a Powerful Animal Comes” appear here as the only archived performances of those songs, making this a unique historical document [1]. The band also played rarer tracks like “Beautiful Gas Mask” and “The Destruction of the Kola Superdeep Borehole Tower,” which have limited archive presence [1]. A highlight includes “The Day the Aliens Came (Hawaiian Feeling),” a bustout not seen in 114 previous archived shows [1]. The performance concludes with a five-song encore, including “Dark in Here” and “Spent Gladiator 2” [1]. This recording is the only available capture of this specific date, offering a complete view of the night’s musical journey [1].",
